00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:45,000
The 13th Warrior is a 1999 American historical fiction action film based on Michael Crichton's 1976 novel Eaters of the Dead, which is
a loose adaptation of the tale of Beowulf combined with Ahmad ibn Fadlan's historical account of the Volga Vikings.

12
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:54,000
It stars Antonio Banderas as Ahmad ibn Fadlan (credited as Ahmed ibn
Fahdlan), as well as Diane Venora and Omar Sharif.

13
01:06:57,000 --> 01:07:03,000
It was directed by John McTiernan; Crichton directed some uncredited reshoots.

14
01:12:06,000 --> 01:12:12,000
The film was produced by McTiernan, Crichton, and Ned Dowd, with Andrew G.

15
01:17:15,000 --> 01:17:21,000
Vajna, James Biggam and Ethan Dubrow as executive producers.

16
01:22:24,000 --> 01:22:30,000
Production and marketing costs reportedly ranged from $100–$160 million, but it grossed $61 million at the box
office worldwide, becoming the biggest box-office bomb of 1999, with losses of up to $129 million.

17
01:27:33,000 --> 01:27:39,000
Despite its critical and box office failure, the film has since cultivated a devoted cult
following, and is credited with pioneering a Muslim hero in Hollywood blockbusters.

18
01:32:42,000 --> 01:32:48,000
The film explores themes of witch, mission, based
on novel or book, kingdom, arabian.

